e space_time is good (0.77, 0.78) but not perfect.\n\nAs a skeptic, I should question:\n1. The suspect description \"two males 30-40 medium build\" is very common - could be coincidence\n2. Cutter is a standard house-breaking tool\n3. No MO match on the second crime (null)\n4. No corroboration\n5. Three crimes in one night across three neighborhoods - possible but need to verify if this is a known pattern or if there are more crimes\n\nThe prior vetted answers show that for similar pairs, the Skeptic sent them back to get MO details. In one prior answer, the Skeptic approved the pair with same station (0.2 km) but sent back the cross-station pair (1.3 km). These are both cross-station pairs at 1.3 km.\n\nI'll send_back both, asking for MO details on the second crimes and possibly a narrower search ring to see if there are more crimes in the immediate vicinity with matching MO.</think>{\n  \"pairs\": {\n    \"CHN-KU-2025-000078|CHN-MG-2025-000079\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"send_back\",\n      \"critique\": \"Strong spatiotemporal proximity (1.3 km, 59 min) and identical generic suspect description (2 males 30-40 medium build) plus same weapon (cutter). However, MO is null on the second crime \u2014 cannot confirm the same cut_window_grille approach or on_foot escape. The suspect description is too common to be distinctive alone. Coverage is low (0.35). Need MO details on CHN-MG-2025-000079 and check for additional crimes in the corridor between Kumaran Nagar and MGR Nagar that night.\",\n      \"requery\": {\n        \"days\": 0,\n        \"ring\": 1,\n        \"note\": \"Re-query with 1 km ring around both locations for 2025-01-19 to find any other night_house_break with cutter and matching MO; request MO details for CHN-MG-2025-000079 from PS-MGRNAGAR-R10.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"CHN-KU-2025-000078|CHN-MG-2025-000077\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"send_back\",\n      \"critique\": \"Same pattern: 1.3 km, 50 min apart, identical generic suspect description and cutter.